Package: artbin
Title: Sample Size and Power for Binary Outcome Trials
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Abdel", "Babiker", role = "aut"),
    person("Patrick", "Royston", role = "aut"),
    person("Friederike", "Barthel", role = "aut"),
    person("Ella", "Marley-Zagar", role = "aut"),
    person("Ian", "White", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "ian.white@ucl.ac.uk")
  )
Description: Calculates sample size and power for clinical trials with binary
    outcomes. Supports superiority, non-inferiority, and substantial-superiority
    designs for two or more treatment arms. Implements score, Wald, and
    conditional (Peto's approximation) tests, with options for continuity
    correction, linear trend tests, loss to follow-up, and unequal allocation.
    Based on the Stata artbin/art2bin programs from the MRC Clinical Trials Unit
    at UCL.
